IMPORT prelude

-- Gas Act 2001 (Singapore) -- the rules a business, contractor, gas worker or consumer actually meets: who needs a gas licence
-- (s 6), who may do gas service work and who may engage them (ss 11-13), building over and moving gas pipes (ss 30, 31), earthworks
-- near gas pipes (s 32), damaging gas plant and submarine pipelines (ss 32A, 32B), meter tampering and theft of gas (s 47),
-- unauthorised reconnection (s 49), notice of meter connection (s 50), restoring a disconnected supply (s 52), on-site safety rules
-- (s 64), officers of a company (s 89), the general penalty (s 91) and composition (s 92).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/GA2001.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 27 of 2024 (latest annotated in force 1 September 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the offences and duties above. Not
-- encoded: the Authority's licensing discretion (s 7), licence conditions, modification and revocation (Part 4), gas transporters'
-- network duties and works powers (Part 5 beyond ss 30-32B), gas allocation and key facilities (ss 38A-38C), entry powers
-- (ss 53-61), the gas importer provisions (ss 61AA, 61AB), the Gas Network Code (Part 7), control of designated licensees (Part 7B),
-- severe gas shortage (Part 8A), competition (Part 9), appeals and transitional provisions.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Gas Act 2001 -- offences and duties`

§§ `6 -- activities that need a gas licence`

-- s 6(1): "no person may" (a) convey gas through a gas pipeline to any premises, or to a transporter's network; (b) "convey gas for
-- or on behalf of a gas transporter (other than as an employee of the gas transporter)"; (c) ship gas, (d) retail gas and (g) produce
-- town gas -- each "on or after such date as the Minister may, by order in the Gazette, specify"; (e) manage or operate an onshore
-- receiving facility; (f) manage or operate an LNG terminal; (ga), (h) import natural gas or LNG; "unless the person is authorised to
-- do so by a gas licence or is exempted under section 8".
-- s 6(2): without a licence a person may (a) "convey, in any premises or part thereof in which that person has an interest, gas
-- supplied for use in the premises" or (b) sell, for use in those premises, gas retailed for use there by a gas retailer.
DECLARE GasActivity IS ONE OF
    `conveying gas through a pipeline to premises`
    `conveying gas for a gas transporter as its employee`
    `conveying gas for a gas transporter as a contractor`
    `conveying gas within premises it has an interest in`
    `reselling retailed gas for use in premises it has an interest in`
    `shipping gas`
    `retailing gas`
    `producing town gas`
    `operating an onshore receiving facility`
    `operating an LNG terminal`
    `importing LNG for its own use`
    `importing natural gas for a prescribed generation entity`

GIVEN `the activity` IS A GasActivity, `the Minister's gazetted date has passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a gas licence is needed` IF
    CONSIDER `the activity`
    WHEN `conveying gas for a gas transporter as its employee` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `conveying gas within premises it has an interest in` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `reselling retailed gas for use in premises it has an interest in` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `shipping gas` THEN `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    WHEN `retailing gas` THEN `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    WHEN `producing town gas` THEN `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 6(6): contravention of (1) -- "a fine not exceeding $1 million and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine not
-- exceeding $25,000 for every day or part of a day". No imprisonment is provided.
GIVEN `the activity` IS A GasActivity, `the Minister's gazetted date has passed` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a gas licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is exempted under section 8` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unlicensed activity is an offence` IF
        `a gas licence is needed` `the activity` `the Minister's gazetted date has passed`
    AND (NOT `holds a gas licence for it`)
    AND (NOT `is exempted under section 8`)

-- s 6(3): a person "not incorporated in Singapore and [without] a place of business in Singapore" may operate an onshore receiving
-- facility as principal without a licence if (a) it appoints a Singapore-incorporated or Singapore-based person to operate it on its
-- behalf "(other than as an employee)" and (b) that person is licensed under (1)(e)(ii).
GIVEN `the principal is foreign with no place of business here` IS A BOOLEAN, `appointed a local operator who is not its employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the local operator is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign principal needs no licence` IF
    `the principal is foreign with no place of business here` AND `appointed a local operator who is not its employee` AND `the local operator is licensed`

§§ `11, 12 and 13 -- gas service work`

-- s 2: "gas service work" means any work on any gas installation or gas appliance, "including any design, construction, installation,
-- commissioning, erection, testing, repair, addition, alteration or maintenance work".
-- s 12(3): the Authority may license a gas service worker; (5) "under different classes for different types of gas service work";
-- (6) a holder of a licence under s 100 of the Public Utilities Act in force immediately before 14 February 2008 is, "unless the
-- Authority directs otherwise, deemed to be a licensed gas service worker".
GIVEN `holds a licence under section 12` IS A BOOLEAN, `held a Public Utilities Act licence before 14 February 2008` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Authority directed otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a licensed gas service worker` IF
        `holds a licence under section 12`
    OR  (`held a Public Utilities Act licence before 14 February 2008` AND (NOT `the Authority directed otherwise`))

-- s 11(1): no person may carry out, or offer or undertake to carry out, gas service work, or hold himself or herself out as a gas
-- service worker, "unless he or she is registered as a professional engineer and has a valid practising certificate under the
-- Professional Engineers Act 1991, or holds a valid gas service worker licence in respect of the specific class of work".
-- (3): the section "does not apply to a gas transporter, a gas transport agent, or an employee" of either. No penalty is expressly
-- provided, so s 91 applies.
GIVEN `is a professional engineer with a practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is licensed for this class of work` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a gas transporter, transport agent or their employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may carry out the gas service work` IF
        `is a professional engineer with a practising certificate`
    OR  `is licensed for this class of work`
    OR  `is a gas transporter, transport agent or their employee`

-- s 13: "Any person who employs or instructs any person who is not a licensed gas service worker to carry out or cause to be carried out
-- any gas service work shall be guilty of an offence." The words are "a licensed gas service worker" -- not "licensed for the class",
-- and with no carve-out for a professional engineer or a transporter's employee. This rule follows the words.
GIVEN `the worker is a licensed gas service worker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `engaging the worker is an offence` IF
    NOT `the worker is a licensed gas service worker`

§§ `30 and 31 -- pipes on private land`

-- s 30(3): a disused gas main or service pipe -- the transporter "may of its own volition or must at the reasonable request of the
-- owner, remove [it] from the land at its own expense". (4): "owner" includes "any person having a leasehold interest with an
-- unexpired term of not less than 7 years".
GIVEN `is the freehold owner` IS A BOOLEAN, `unexpired lease in years` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may require removal of a disused pipe` IF
    `is the freehold owner` OR `unexpired lease in years` AT LEAST 7

-- s 31(1): "No person may build, erect or construct anything over any existing gas transmission pipeline, gas main or gas service pipe
-- ... without the approval of the gas transporter." (2): an owner or occupier whose premises have a structure over a pipe "must have
-- [it] relocated or diverted away". (3): the cost is borne (a) by the owner or occupier "to the extent that [they] benefit", or where
-- the structure was built by them in contravention of (1); and (b) "by the gas transporter in all other circumstances".
DECLARE CostBearer IS ONE OF
    `the owner or occupier`
    `the owner or occupier to the extent of the benefit, otherwise the gas transporter`
    `the gas transporter`

GIVEN `the owner or occupier built it without approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner or occupier benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CostBearer
`who pays to divert the pipe` MEANS
    IF `the owner or occupier built it without approval`
    THEN `the owner or occupier`
    ELSE `who pays where built with approval` `the owner or occupier benefits`

GIVEN `the owner or occupier benefits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CostBearer
`who pays where built with approval` MEANS
    IF `the owner or occupier benefits`
    THEN `the owner or occupier to the extent of the benefit, otherwise the gas transporter`
    ELSE `the gas transporter`

§§ `32 -- earthworks near gas pipes`

-- s 32(1): no person may commence or carry out earthworks "within the vicinity of any gas plant or gas pipe" of a gas transporter unless
-- the person (a) "has given to the gas transporter not less than 7 days' notice in writing", (b) has obtained the location of the plant
-- or pipe, and (c) has consulted the transporter on preventing damage. (2): the Authority "may ... modify the period". (5): nothing in
-- (1) stops earthworks where the person "has reasonable cause to believe that it is necessary to do so in the interest of public or
-- private safety"; (6) but they must give written notice "not more than 24 hours after". (5A): (1) does not bind the transporter on
-- its own network.
GIVEN `the Authority modified the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the modified period in days` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earthworks notice period in days` MEANS
    IF `the Authority modified the period` THEN `the modified period in days` ELSE 7

GIVEN `is the gas transporter on its own network` IS A BOOLEAN, `believes it necessary for safety` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days of written notice given` IS A NUMBER, `the Authority modified the period` IS A BOOLEAN, `the modified period in days` IS A NUMBER,
      `obtained the pipe location` IS A BOOLEAN, `consulted the gas transporter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may commence the earthworks` IF
        `is the gas transporter on its own network`
    OR  `believes it necessary for safety`
    OR  (    `days of written notice given` AT LEAST `the earthworks notice period in days` `the Authority modified the period` `the modified period in days`
         AND `obtained the pipe location`
         AND `consulted the gas transporter`)

GIVEN `hours after starting when notice was given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the emergency earthworks notice was in time` IF
    `hours after starting when notice was given` AT MOST 24

-- s 32(8): defence "to prove (a) that the person took all reasonable steps to discharge the person's duty ... or (b) ... took all
-- reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence". (9): if the defence "involves acting on information supplied by" a gas
-- transporter (or an infrastructure owner), the accused may not rely on it "without permission of the court" unless he served a
-- written notice identifying the supplier on the prosecutor "within 14 clear days before the hearing". s 32A(4), (5) are the same for
-- damage under s 32A(1)(a), (b).
GIVEN `proved reasonable steps or due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the defence relies on information from the gas transporter` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `clear days before the hearing the notice was served` IS A NUMBER, `the court gave permission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the due diligence defence is available` IF
        `proved reasonable steps or due diligence`
    AND (    (NOT `the defence relies on information from the gas transporter`)
         OR  `clear days before the hearing the notice was served` AT LEAST 14
         OR  `the court gave permission`)

§§ `32A and 32B -- damaging gas plant and submarine pipelines`

-- s 32A(1): any person who (a) "removes, destroys or damages any gas plant or gas pipe" of a gas licensee, (b) causes or permits it, or
-- (c) otherwise "wilfully or recklessly hinders or prevents" its use, is guilty of an offence. (a) and (b) carry no mental element; the
-- only answer is the (4) due diligence defence, which does not extend to (c).
-- s 32B: any person who "wilfully, recklessly or negligently" damages or is likely to damage a submarine gas pipeline in Singapore's
-- territorial waters, or omits to prevent it. No defence is stated.
DECLARE MentalState IS ONE OF
    `without fault`
    `negligently`
    `recklessly`
    `wilfully`

GIVEN `the state of mind` IS A MentalState
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wilful or reckless` IF
    CONSIDER `the state of mind`
    WHEN `wilfully` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `recklessly` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `damaged the plant or pipe` IS A BOOLEAN, `the state of mind` IS A MentalState, `the defence is available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the onshore damage is an offence` IF
    IF `damaged the plant or pipe`
    THEN NOT `the defence is available`
    ELSE `wilful or reckless` `the state of mind`

GIVEN `the state of mind` IS A MentalState
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the submarine pipeline damage is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the state of mind`
    WHEN `without fault` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `47 -- theft of gas and meter tampering`

-- s 47(4): a person is "presumed, until the contrary is proved" to have tampered with a meter if it is proved that at the time (a)(i) a
-- device was attached to or near it, (ii) its covering "had a hole which is not a result of ordinary wear and tear", (iii) a licensee's
-- seal or lock was damaged, removed or changed, or (iv) a licensee's paint or chemical marking was damaged or removed; "and" (b) the
-- person "had ... custody or control of the meter".
GIVEN `a device was attached to or near the meter` IS A BOOLEAN, `the cover had a hole not from wear and tear` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a licensee's seal or lock was damaged, removed or changed` IS A BOOLEAN, `a licensee's paint marking was damaged or removed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `had custody or control of the meter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tampering is presumed` IF
        (   `a device was attached to or near the meter`
         OR `the cover had a hole not from wear and tear`
         OR `a licensee's seal or lock was damaged, removed or changed`
         OR `a licensee's paint marking was damaged or removed`)
    AND `had custody or control of the meter`

§§ `50 -- notice of connecting or disconnecting a meter`

-- s 50(1): no person may connect a meter or internal pipe to a gas pipeline, or disconnect it, "unless the person has given 48 hours'
-- notice in the prescribed form" -- (c) to the gas shipper or gas retailer where gas is supplied by one; (d) "in any other case, to the
-- gas transporter". (5): fine not exceeding $5,000.
DECLARE NoticeRecipient IS ONE OF
    `the gas shipper or gas retailer`
    `the gas transporter`

GIVEN `gas is supplied by a shipper or retailer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NoticeRecipient
`who must be given the connection notice` MEANS
    IF `gas is supplied by a shipper or retailer` THEN `the gas shipper or gas retailer` ELSE `the gas transporter`

GIVEN `hours of notice given` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the connection notice is long enough` IF
    `hours of notice given` AT LEAST 48

§§ `52 -- restoring a disconnected supply`

-- s 52(2): the transporter, shipper or retailer is "not under any obligation" to reconnect or restore supply until (a) "the consumer is no
-- longer the owner or occupier of the premises"; or (b) the consumer (i) "has made good the default" and (ii) "has paid the reasonable
-- expenses of disconnecting and re-connecting".
GIVEN `the consumer has left the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `made good the default` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid the reconnection expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the supplier must restore supply` IF
    `the consumer has left the premises` OR (`made good the default` AND `paid the reconnection expenses`)

§§ `64 -- safety on the job`

-- s 64(5): no one working on a gas fitting that exposes a part containing flammable gas "may smoke or use any source of ignition unless
-- the gas installation has been purged ... or has otherwise been made safe". (6): no one searching for an escape "may use any source of
-- ignition unless the source of ignition is incorporated as part of an instrument designed for the detection of gas". (7): "No person
-- may use any naked flame or carry out any hotwork in the vicinity where gas is known to be leaking" -- no exception.
DECLARE IgnitionSituation IS ONE OF
    `working on an exposed gas fitting`
    `searching for a gas escape`
    `near a known gas leak`

GIVEN `the situation` IS A IgnitionSituation, `the installation was purged or made safe` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the ignition is part of a gas detector` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a source of ignition may be used` IF
    CONSIDER `the situation`
    WHEN `working on an exposed gas fitting` THEN `the installation was purged or made safe`
    WHEN `searching for a gas escape` THEN `the ignition is part of a gas detector`
    WHEN `near a known gas leak` THEN FALSE

§§ `89 -- officers of a company`

-- s 89: where a body of persons commits an offence, a director, manager, secretary or similar officer or partner "shall be guilty of
-- that offence ... unless the person proves that (a) the offence was committed without the person's consent or connivance; and (b) the
-- person had exercised all such due diligence".
GIVEN `the company committed an offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `was an officer or partner` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no consent or connivance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proved due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
        `the company committed an offence`
    AND `was an officer or partner`
    AND (NOT (`proved no consent or connivance` AND `proved due diligence`))

§§ `Penalties -- ss 6, 32, 32A, 32B, 47, 49, 50, 64, 91 and 92`

-- s 6(6) $1 million, + $25,000 a day; s 32(7) $100,000 or 5 years; s 32A(1) $1 million or 5 years; s 32B $2 million or 5 years;
-- s 47(2) "an amount not exceeding $50,000; and an amount equal to 3 times the value of gas", or 5 years, + $250 a day; s 49(1)(a)
-- $10,000 or 3 years; s 50(5) $5,000; s 64(8) $50,000 or 5 years, + $250 a day.
-- s 91: an offence "for which no penalty is expressly provided" -- $10,000 or 12 months, + $250 a day (ss 11, 13, 31, 40, 41, 42).
-- Daily further fines run "for every day or part of a day during which the offence continues after conviction".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `unlicensed gas activity`
    `unlicensed gas service work`
    `engaging an unlicensed gas service worker`
    `building over a gas pipe`
    `earthworks without notice`
    `damaging gas plant`
    `damaging a submarine gas pipeline`
    `meter tampering or gas theft`
    `reconnecting without consent`
    `connecting a meter without notice`
    `breaching a gas safety rule`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `value of gas taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed gas activity` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `earthworks without notice` THEN 100000
    WHEN `damaging gas plant` THEN 1000000
    WHEN `damaging a submarine gas pipeline` THEN 2000000
    WHEN `meter tampering or gas theft` THEN 50000 PLUS 3 TIMES `value of gas taken`
    WHEN `connecting a meter without notice` THEN 5000
    WHEN `breaching a gas safety rule` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 10000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed gas activity` THEN 0
    WHEN `connecting a meter without notice` THEN 0
    WHEN `reconnecting without consent` THEN 36
    WHEN `earthworks without notice` THEN 60
    WHEN `damaging gas plant` THEN 60
    WHEN `damaging a submarine gas pipeline` THEN 60
    WHEN `meter tampering or gas theft` THEN 60
    WHEN `breaching a gas safety rule` THEN 60
    OTHERWISE 12

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the further fine per day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `unlicensed gas activity` THEN 25000
    WHEN `meter tampering or gas theft` THEN 250
    WHEN `breaching a gas safety rule` THEN 250
    WHEN `unlicensed gas service work` THEN 250
    WHEN `engaging an unlicensed gas service worker` THEN 250
    WHEN `building over a gas pipe` THEN 250
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `value of gas taken` IS A NUMBER, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the total maximum fine` MEANS
    `the maximum fine` `the offence` `value of gas taken` PLUS `the further fine per day` `the offence` TIMES `days continuing after conviction`

-- s 92(1): the Authority may compound a prescribed compoundable offence "by collecting ... a sum not exceeding $3,000". Which offences
-- are compoundable is left to regulations (s 92(2)), not retrieved.
GIVEN `the sum proposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the composition sum is within the cap` IF
    `the sum proposed` AT MOST 3000
